{"strongs": "H8045", "word": "שָׁמַד", "translit": "sha.mad", "root": "שמד", "morph": "H:V", "pos": "verb Niph`al", "gloss": "be exterminated, destroyed", "definition": "[ שָׁמַד ] 90 verb Niph`al be exterminated, destroyed (Late Hebrew derived species; Aramaic שְׁמַד Pa`el cause to apostatize ( Jastr ); Syriac seems disputed (in Lexicons); Nö Eut. Nab. 32 curse ; Ba ES 10 cites Assyrian ašmud , I destroyed ; Gerber 112 thinks verb denominative); — Perfect 3 masculine singular consecutive וְנִשְׁמַד Ezek 32:12 +, etc.; Imperfect 3 masculine singular יִשָּׁמֵ Isa 48:19 ; Prov 14:11 2 masculine plural תִּשָּׁמֵד֑וּן Deut 4:26 Infinitiveabsolute הִשָּׁמֵד v Deut 4:26 construct suffix הִשָּׁמֶדְךָ Deut 28:20 , etc.; — 1. of person be annihilated, exterminated , Gen 34:30 ( J ), Judg 21:16 ; 2Sam 21:5 (+ מֵהִתְיַצֵּב בְּ ; — but read לְהַשְׁמִידֵגוּ ᵐ5 Ew We Dr and others), Ps 37:38 (|| נִכְדָת ), Ps 83:11 of people Deut 4:26 ( ׳ הִשָּׁמֵד תּשּׁ ), Deut 7:23 ; Deut 12:30 (+ מִפָּנֶתךָ Deut 28:20 (|| אָבַד v Deut 28:24 v Deut 28:45 v Deut 28:51 v Deut 28:61 , Jer 48:42 (+ מֵעִם . Ezek 33:12 ; Ps 92:8 (+ עֲדֵיעַֿד , compare also וְלֹא יִשָּׁמֵד שְׁמוֺ מִלְּפָנָי֑ Isa 48:19 (+ יִכָרֵת ; וַרְעֶ֑ךָ etc., in || clause). 2. be destroyed , of bamoth, Hos 10:8 , compare ( בֵּית רְשָׁעִים ) Prov 14:11 be devastated , of land, Jer 48:8 (|| אבר ). Hiph`il 69 Perfect 3 masculine singular הִשְׁמִיד Deut 2:22 +, etc.; Imperfect 3 masculine singular יַשְׁמִיד Isa 13:9 +, וַיַּשְׁמֵד 1Kgs 16:12 ; 2Kgs 10:28 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular הַשְׁמֵד Deut 33:27 Infinitive absolute הַשְׁמֵד Isa 14:28 , יֵ֯ד Amos 9:8 construct לְהַשְׁמִיר Josh 9:24 +, also עַד הִשְׁמִידְךָ Deut 7:24 , וֺ - Deut 28:48 , ָ֯ ם - Josh 11:14 (but read in all ׳ הַשׁ , as Josh 23:15 , see Dr Deut 7:24 ), לַשְׁמִד Isa 23:11 , etc.; — 1. annihilate, exterminate: accusative of person or a people, subject ׳ י or human person, Deut 1:27 ; Deut 2:22 (+ מִפְּנֵי person), Deut 6:15 (+ מֵעַלפְּֿנֵי הָאֲרָמָה ), Deut 9:20 + 16 t. Deuteronomy; Josh 7:12 (accusative הַחֵרֶם ; + מִקִּרְבְּכֶם ), Josh 9:24 +4 t. Joshua (all R D ), 2Kgs 14:16 ; 1Kgs 13:34 ; Amos 9:8 ; Isa 13:9 ; Isa 26:14 ; Esth 3:6 ; Esth 3:13 + 23 t.; accusative פִּרְיוֺ וְשָׁרָשָׁיו (figurative) Amos 2:9 , compare Ezek 34:16 (but Vrss Co Toy and others [not Hi Krae ] אֶשְׁמֹר ); אֶתשְֿׁמִי ׳ הִשׁ 1Sam 24:22 ( Gi v. 1Sam 24:21 ), 2Sam 22:38 ; 1Kgs 16:12 ; Ps 145:20 הַשְׁמֵד as substantive, Isa 14:23 besom of extermination ; accusative אֶתהַֿבַּעַל 2Kgs 10:28 , of extirpating Baal-worship מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל . 2. destroy , cities Mic 5:13 , fortresses Isa 23:11 , bamoth Lev 26:30 ( H ), Num 33:52 ( P ; || אִבֵּד ), חֹזֶק מַמְלְכוֺת הַגּוֺיִם Hag 2:22 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8787')\">BDB8787</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H8045')\">H8045</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8786')\">BDB8786</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB8788')\">BDB8788</entry></div><p> [<bdbheb>שָׁמַד</bdbheb>]<sub>90</sub> <b>verb Niph`al</b> <highlightword>be exterminated, destroyed</highlightword> (Late Hebrew derived species; Aramaic <bdbarc>שְׁמַד</bdbarc> Pa`el <highlight>cause to apostatize</highlight> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Jastr')\">Jastr</lookup>); Syriac <placeholder5600/> seems disputed (in Lexicons); <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Nö')\">Nö<sup>Eut. Nab. 32</sup></lookup> <highlight>curse</highlight>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ba')\">Ba<sup>ES 10</sup></lookup> cites Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>ašmud</highlight></transliteration>, <highlight>I destroyed</highlight>; <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Gerber')\">Gerber<sup>112</sup></lookup> thinks verb denominative); — <highlight>Perfect 3 masculine singular consecutive</highlight> <bdbheb>וְנִשְׁמַד</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 32:12\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(26,32,12)\">Ezek 32:12</ref> +, etc.; <highlight>Imperfect</highlight> 3 masculine singular <bdbheb>יִשָּׁמֵ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 48:19\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(23,48,19)\">Isa 48:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 14:11\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(20,14,11)\">Prov 14:11</ref> 2 masculine plural <bdbheb>תִּשָּׁמֵד֑וּן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 4:26\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(5,4,26)\">Deut 4:26</ref> <highlight>Infinitiveabsolute</highlight> <bdbheb>הִשָּׁמֵד</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Deut 4:26\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(5,4,26)\">Deut 4:26</ref> construct suffix <bdbheb>הִשָּׁמֶדְךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 28:20\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,20)\">Deut 28:20</ref>, etc.; — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> of person <highlight>be annihilated, exterminated</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Gen 34:30\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(1,34,30)\">Gen 34:30</ref> (<lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('J')\"><reflink>J</reflink></lookup>), <ref ref=\"Judg 21:16\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(7,21,16)\">Judg 21:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 21:5\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(10,21,5)\">2Sam 21:5</ref> (+ <bdbheb>מֵהִתְיַצֵּב בְּ</bdbheb>; — but read <bdbheb>לְהַשְׁמִידֵגוּ</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Ew')\">Ew</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('We')\">We</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Dr')\">Dr</lookup> and others), <ref ref=\"Ps 37:38\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"38\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"38\" onclick=\"bcv(19,37,38)\">Ps 37:38</ref> (|| <bdbheb>נִכְדָת</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Ps 83:11\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"83\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"83\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(19,83,11)\">Ps 83:11</ref> of people <ref ref=\"Deut 4:26\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(5,4,26)\">Deut 4:26</ref> (<bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>הִשָּׁמֵד תּשּׁ</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Deut 7:23\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(5,7,23)\">Deut 7:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 12:30\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"30\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"30\" onclick=\"bcv(5,12,30)\">Deut 12:30</ref>(+ <bdbheb>מִפָּנֶתךָ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Deut 28:20\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,20)\">Deut 28:20</ref> (|| <bdbheb>אָבַד</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Deut 28:24\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,24)\">Deut 28:24</ref> v<ref ref=\"Deut 28:45\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"45\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"45\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,45)\">Deut 28:45</ref> v<ref ref=\"Deut 28:51\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"51\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"51\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,51)\">Deut 28:51</ref> v<ref ref=\"Deut 28:61\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"61\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"61\" onclick=\"bcv(5,28,61)\">Deut 28:61</ref>, <ref ref=\"Jer 48:42\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"42\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"42\" onclick=\"bcv(24,48,42)\">Jer 48:42</ref> (+<bdbheb>מֵעִם</bdbheb>. <ref ref=\"Ezek 33:12\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(26,33,12)\">Ezek 33:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 92:8\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"92\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"92\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(19,92,8)\">Ps 92:8</ref> (+ <bdbheb>עֲדֵיעַֿד</bdbheb>, compare also <bdbheb>וְלֹא יִשָּׁמֵד שְׁמוֺ מִלְּפָנָי֑</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 48:19\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"48\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"48\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(23,48,19)\">Isa 48:19</ref> (+ <bdbheb>יִכָרֵת</bdbheb>; <bdbheb>וַרְעֶ֑ךָ</bdbheb> etc., in || clause). </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> <highlight>be destroyed</highlight>, of bamoth, <ref ref=\"Hos 10:8\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(28,10,8)\">Hos 10:8</ref>, compare (<bdbheb>בֵּית רְשָׁעִים</